       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. The usual OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day, a common prescription maximum)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the absolute ceiling)\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll reconsider. I'd want a note on the order with your rationale. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
